Package: randomMachines
Title: Weighted Ensembles of Kernel Support Vector Machines
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("First", "Last", , "first.last@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits Random Machines, a support vector machine ensemble that
    draws on several kernel functions rather than committing to one. Fitting
    runs in two stages. A cross-validation stage scores each candidate kernel
    and maps its performance to a selection probability (lambda); a bootstrap
    stage fits one lambda-sampled kernel per resample and weights the fitted
    models by their out-of-bag performance (omega). Prediction aggregates the
    bootstrap models by their weights, yielding a weighted majority vote, an
    averaged class-probability matrix, or a weighted mean for binary,
    multiclass, probabilistic and regression tasks.
